cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "IIOAC Fugitive Source: a browser port of EPA's Indoor and Outdoor Air Calculator"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Jeet
repository-code: "https://github.com/JeetDSharma/iioac"
url: "https://iioac.vercel.app/"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22101723
abstract: >-
  A browser implementation of the fugitive-source path of the U.S. EPA Indoor
  and Outdoor Air Calculator (IIOAC 1.0), replacing the macro-enabled Excel
  workbook with a self-contained web page. Given source parameters and emission
  scenarios it reports outdoor and indoor air concentrations, wet, dry and total
  deposition, and acute, chronic and lifetime inhalation doses for seven
  receptor age groups at fenceline, outer-boundary and community locations.
  All calculation runs client-side. Results are validated against an independent
  oracle that parses the original workbook's formulas and AERMOD run files,
  agreeing to within 5.7e-08 relative error, the float32 storage limit of the
  archived dispersion data. Not affiliated with or endorsed by the U.S. EPA.
keywords:
  - air quality
  - dispersion modeling
  - AERMOD
  - exposure assessment
  - risk assessment
  - inhalation dose
  - EPA
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-25"
